    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Assignment 2 — Data Objects, Attribute Types & Statistical Descriptions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Dataset:** HR_comma_sep.csv (14,995 employee records)  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Tools:** Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn, SciPy  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Course:** Data Analytics — B.Tech ECE\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Overview\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook analyzes the HR employee dataset across four parts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part A:** Data object classification (quantitative, categorical, binary)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part B:** Central tendency & dispersion (mean, median, variance, IQR, CV)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part C:** Univariate & multivariate analysis (histogram, box plot, Q-Q plot, pairplot, correlation)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part D:** Analytics dashboard (4 charts — Python alternative to Tableau/Power BI)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Key Finding:** High-performing but dissatisfied employees who work excessive hours (250+/month) are the most likely to leave — indicating burnout-driven attrition.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Setup — Install & Load\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Install gdown for Google Drive downloads\\n\",\n",
    "    \"!pip install -q gdown\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Download dataset from Google Drive\\n\",\n",
    "    \"!gdown \\\"https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1bviXba_EF5Sqv_RzUUtquON5KUrdrjjj\\\" -O \\\"HR_comma_sep.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Import libraries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import scipy.stats as stats\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from IPython.display import display, Markdown\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load and clean column names\\n\",\n",
    "    \"url_hr = \\\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bviXba_EF5Sqv_RzUUtquON5KUrdrjjj/view?usp=sharing\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df = pd.read_csv(url_hr)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df.columns = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"              'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company', 'Work_accident',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"              'left', 'promotion_last_5years', 'Department', 'salary']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Shape: {df.shape}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Columns: {list(df.columns)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df.head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part A — Data Object Classification [4 Marks]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Classification Table\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"classification = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"Data Type\\\": [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Quantitative — Continuous\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Quantitative — Discrete\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Categorical — Nominal\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Categorical — Ordinal\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Binary (Dichotomous)\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"Columns\\\": [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"satisfaction_level, last_evaluation, average_montly_hours\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"number_project, time_spend_company\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Department\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"salary\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"left, Work_accident, promotion_last_5years\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"Justification\\\": [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Continuous numeric measurements with meaningful arithmetic operations.\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Discrete numeric values (counts/years). Support arithmetic but integer-only.\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Named categories with no inherent ordering (sales, hr, IT, etc.).\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Categories (low, medium, high) with natural ordering.\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"Binary attributes encoded as 0/1 indicating presence/absence.\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(classification)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part B — Central Tendency & Dispersion [6 Marks]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Statistical Summary Table\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"numeric_cols = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"stats_table = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col: {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Mean': round(df[col].mean(), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Median': round(df[col].median(), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Mode': round(df[col].mode().iloc[0], 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Range': round(df[col].max() - df[col].min(), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Variance': round(df[col].var(), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Std Dev': round(df[col].std(), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'IQR': round(df[col].quantile(0.75) - df[col].quantile(0.25), 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'CV (%)': round((df[col].std() / df[col].mean()) * 100, 2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    } for col in numeric_cols\\n\",\n",
    "    \"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(stats_table.style.set_table_attributes('style=\\\"font-size: 11px\\\"'))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Dispersion Commentary\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for col in numeric_cols:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cv = (df[col].std() / df[col].mean()) * 100\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    level = \\\"HIGHLY DISPERSED\\\" if cv > 50 else \\\"MODERATELY DISPERSED\\\" if cv > 25 else \\\"TIGHTLY CLUSTERED\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{col}: CV = {cv:.2f}% → {level}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part C — Univariate & Multivariate Analysis [5 Marks]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### C1: Univariate Analysis — `satisfaction_level`\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Histogram\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.hist(df['satisfaction_level'], bins=30, edgecolor='black', color='skyblue', alpha=0.85)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.axvline(df['satisfaction_level'].mean(), color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=f\\\"Mean: {df['satisfaction_level'].mean():.3f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.axvline(df['satisfaction_level'].median(), color='green', linestyle='--', linewidth=2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=f\\\"Median: {df['satisfaction_level'].median():.3f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Histogram of Employee Satisfaction Level', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Satisfaction Level')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Frequency')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(axis='y', alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Distribution: Bimodal — peaks near 0.1 and 0.8\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Skewness: {df['satisfaction_level'].skew():.4f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Box Plot\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(6, 7))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.boxplot(df['satisfaction_level'], vert=True, patch_artist=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            boxprops=dict(facecolor='lightblue', edgecolor='navy', linewidth=2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            medianprops=dict(color='red', linewidth=2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            whiskerprops=dict(color='navy', linewidth=1.5),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            capprops=dict(color='navy', linewidth=1.5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Box Plot of Satisfaction Level', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Satisfaction Level')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xticks([1], ['Satisfaction'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(axis='y', alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Q1, Q3 = df['satisfaction_level'].quantile(0.25), df['satisfaction_level'].quantile(0.75)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IQR = Q3 - Q1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Q1: {Q1:.3f} | Q3: {Q3:.3f} | IQR: {IQR:.3f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Outliers (IQR method): {len(df[(df['satisfaction_level'] < Q1-1.5*IQR) | (df['satisfaction_level'] > Q3+1.5*IQR)])}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Q-Q Plot\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(8, 7))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"stats.probplot(df['satisfaction_level'], dist=\\\"norm\\\", plot=plt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Q-Q Plot of Satisfaction Level', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"skew = df['satisfaction_level'].skew()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Skewness: {skew:.4f} → {'Left-skewed (tail toward low satisfaction)' if skew < 0 else 'Right-skewed'}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Deviation from diagonal confirms non-normal (bimodal) distribution.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### C2: Multivariate Analysis — Pairplot\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"sample = df.sample(n=2000, random_state=42)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"g = sns.pairplot(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sample[['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company', 'left']],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    hue='left', palette='coolwarm',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plot_kws={'alpha': 0.6, 's': 30},\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    diag_kind='kde', height=2.5\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"g.fig.suptitle('Pair Plot — Numeric Attributes (Color-coded by Attrition)', y=1.02, fontsize=13)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\nKey Observations:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"1. Departed employees cluster at LOW satisfaction + HIGH evaluation\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"2. HIGH monthly hours + LOW satisfaction → attrition (burnout pattern)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"3. More projects → more hours; departed employees in 4-7 project range\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### C3: Correlation Analysis\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"corr, p_val = stats.pearsonr(df['last_evaluation'], df['number_project'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Pearson Correlation (r): {corr:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"p-value: {p_val:.2e}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"R²: {corr**2 * 100:.2f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"strength = 'Strong' if abs(corr) > 0.7 else 'Moderate' if abs(corr) > 0.4 else 'Weak'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nInterpretation: {strength} positive correlation\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"→ Employees with more projects receive higher evaluations\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"→ Project involvement is linked to performance recognition\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.scatterplot(data=df.sample(n=3000, random_state=42),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                x='number_project', y='last_evaluation',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                hue='left', palette='coolwarm', alpha=0.5, s=40)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title(f'Evaluation vs Projects (r = {corr:.3f})', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Number of Projects')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Last Evaluation Score')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part D — Analytics Dashboard [5 Marks]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*(Python alternative to Tableau/Power BI)*\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(20, 14))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.suptitle('HR Analytics Dashboard — Employee Attrition Insights', fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', y=0.98)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Chart 1: Attrition by Department\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1 = plt.subplot(2, 2, 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.crosstab(df['Department'], df['left']).plot(kind='bar', ax=ax1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                                                color=['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c'], edgecolor='black')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.set_title('Employees Left vs Stayed by Department', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.set_ylabel('Count')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.legend(title='Status')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Chart 2: Satisfaction by Salary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2 = plt.subplot(2, 2, 2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for s in ['low', 'medium', 'high']:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax2.hist(df[df['salary']==s]['satisfaction_level'], bins=25, alpha=0.6, label=s.capitalize(), edgecolor='black')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.axvline(df['satisfaction_level'].mean(), color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=f'Mean: {df[\\\"satisfaction_level\\\"].mean():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_title('Satisfaction Distribution by Salary Band', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_xlabel('Satisfaction Level')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Chart 3: Evaluation vs Hours\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3 = plt.subplot(2, 2, 3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plot_df = df.sample(n=5000, random_state=42)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sc = ax3.scatter(plot_df['average_montly_hours'], plot_df['last_evaluation'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                 c=plot_df['left'], cmap='coolwarm', alpha=0.5, s=25, edgecolors='none')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3.set_title('Evaluation vs Monthly Hours (by Attrition)', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3.set_xlabel('Average Monthly Hours')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3.set_ylabel('Last Evaluation')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3.legend(*sc.legend_elements(), title=\\\"Left\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Chart 4: Box Plot by Dept\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax4 = plt.subplot(2, 2, 4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_copy = df.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_copy['Status'] = df_copy['left'].map({0: 'Stayed', 1: 'Left'})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.boxplot(data=df_copy, x='Department', y='satisfaction_level',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            hue='Status', ax=ax4, palette='coolwarm',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            flierprops=dict(marker='o', markersize=3, alpha=0.3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax4.set_title('Satisfaction by Department & Status', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax4.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax4.legend(title='Status')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0, 1, 0.96])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Key HR Insights Summary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Burnout of High Performers:** Departed employees had low satisfaction (~0.44) but high evaluations (~0.78) and worked 257+ hrs/month\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Salary drives satisfaction:** Low-salary employees show bimodal split — very unhappy or surprisingly happy\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Workload–Attrition link:** 5+ projects + 250+ hrs/month → significantly higher attrition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Universal pattern:** Satisfaction gap consistent across all 10 departments\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. **Critical tenure window:** Most attrition at 3–5 years\\n\",\n",
    "    \"6. **Evaluation bias:** Weak correlation (r=0.35) between projects and evaluations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*Notebook for Assignment 2 — Data Analytics, B.Tech ECE*\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
